{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And prepare for me savory food.</b> He desired the savory food so that he might engage in the honor of his father, and through this the blessing would rest upon him. For even though he did not recognize the full measure of Esau's wickedness, nevertheless he did not consider him worthy that the blessing he intended to bestow should rest upon him. Therefore when he afterward blessed Jacob — once he knew him to be worthy of blessing — he did not ask for savory food nor request anything, but blessed him immediately, saying: וְאֵל שַׁדַּי יְבָרֵךְ אֹתְךָ (Genesis 28:3)."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:31:55.734471362Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}